-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Flegr</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><article-title>Decrease of psychomotor performance in subjects with latent 'asymptomatic' toxoplasmosis</article-title><source>Parasitology</source><year>2001</year><volume>122</volume><fpage>515</fpage><lpage>520</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11393824</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B7"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Flegr</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Havl&#x000ed;&#x0010d;ek</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Kodym</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Mal&#x000fd;</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Smahel</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><article-title>Increased risk of traffic accidents in subjects with latent toxoplasmosis: a retrospective case-control study</article-title><source>BMC Infect Dis</source><year>2002</year><volume>2</volume><comment>art-11</comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12095427</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B8"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Yereli</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Balcioglu</surname><given-names>IC</given-names></name><name><surname>Ozbilgin</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><article-title>-Is <italic>Toxoplasma gondii </italic>a potential risk for traffic accidents in Turkey?</article-title><source>Forensic Sci Int</source><year>2006</year><volume>163</volume><fpage>34</fpage><lpage>37</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.forsciint.2005.11.002</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16332418</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B9"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Novotn&#x000e1;</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Havl&#x000ed;&#x0010d;ek</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>AP</given-names></name><name><surname>